# Write a service

Trellis projects are authored with `contract.trellis` or `contracts/*.trellis`. The compiler validates those sources, emits canonical API and participant artifacts, and generates private TypeScript or Rust SDKs.

1. [Set up the project](/guides/write-a-service/setup)
2. [Declare the API and participant](/guides/write-a-service/first-contract)
3. [Connect the generated service](/guides/write-a-service/service-entrypoint)
4. [Generate SDKs and artifacts](/guides/write-a-service/contract-artifacts)
5. [Use the development loop](/guides/write-a-service/development-loop)

The [Trellis IDL reference](/guides/write-a-service/first-contract) covers RPCs, operations, events, feeds, state, jobs, and resources.
